### Home page from an external HTML file
# Run: curl localhost:8080/
GET /

< index.html

### Home page by its file name
# Run: curl localhost:8080/index.html
GET /index.html

< index.html

### Embedded HTML page
# Run: curl localhost:8080/index2.html
GET /index2.html
Content-Type: text/html; charset=utf-8

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>Mock Docs 2</title>
</head>
<body>
    <h1>Welcome to Mock Docs 2</h1>
    <p>Hello, World 2!</p>
</body>
</html>

### Text from an external file
# Run: curl localhost:8080/chords
GET /chords

< chords.txt

### Embedded plain text
# Run: curl localhost:8080/chords2
GET /chords2
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8

          --- Chord Tones ---

Chord       Major       Minor       7th
-------     -------     -------     ----
C           C,E,G       C,Eb,G      Bb
D           D,F#,A      D,F,A       C
E           E,G#,B      E,G,B       D
F           F,A,C       F,Ab,C      Eb
G           G,B,D       G,Bb,D      F
A           A,C#,E      A,C,E       G
B           B,D#,F#     B,D,F#      A

Major chord - made up of the 1,3, and 5 note in that key's scale
Minor chord - flat the 3rd note of the scale
Augmented chord - sharp the 5th note of the scale
7th - flat the 7th note of the scale

### Status page
# Run: curl localhost:8080/status
GET /status
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "status": "ok",
    "uptime": "13:34  up 8 days, 33 mins"
}

### Page after a delay
# Run: curl -w '\n%{time_total}s\n' localhost:8080/delay
@delay = 1500ms
GET /delay
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "ok",
  "message": "A bit delayed, right?"
}
